     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"DE-CH\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Dear all,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">exactly one year ago (though with publication date 2021!), Volume 2 of our statistical-ecology textbook &quot;Applied hierarchical modelling in ecology&quot; (AHM2) was published\r\n by Academic Press.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Now we have finally managed to create the accompanying book website, which briefly presents both the AHM1 and the AHM2 book, along with the whole AHMecology project\r\n and the philosophy of hierarchical statistical models. The website also contains further information, links and downloads.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792493776691000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_zGJMhLASMcVGdzjMke-1\">https://www.mbr-pwrc.usgs.gov/pubanalysis/keryroylebook/</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">We owe a very big thank-you to Jim Hines for creating and maintaining the page.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\">Best regards --- Marc, Andy and Mike<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
